                <pb facs="0455" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg357"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Iddings to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-08-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                    1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Iddings reports that the Italian Government has not replied to the indirect
                    communications of cables it has received from Earl Li Hung Chang, dated August
                    19 and 21. His authority to negotiate not being yet defined, they consider his
                    suggestions premature. They think the basis of negotiations should first be
                    settled between the powers.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
